}], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"020926fc-ea84-4dc1-934c-9f43dd102db8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Only in non coordinate system we can have nonvanishing  Lie brackets. \
Choose one coordinate system form above list and define corresponding to have \
gaCoordinateChart[]. \n",
 StyleBox["PROBLEM to understand",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ". Why the Lie coefficient is not a scalar. It is in fact vector. It is easy \
to see that when one take commutator of vectors then we always get scalar + \
bivector. Scalar part have to vanish, because of commutator. What remains is \
always bivector. Not vector! In fact our previous attempts instead of vectors \
we used bivectors (for gaStructureConstant[]). Since in fact bivectors plays \
the role of generators in GA. Why Shindler uses vectors??? "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da11272d-37bf-49f9-a950-460ec3169f83"],

